      "text": "To determine the number of positive divisors of a given number, we first need to find its prime factorization.\n\nStarting with the number 24:\n1. \\(24 \\div 2 = 12\\), so we have \\(24 = 2 \\times 12\\).\n2. \\(12 \\div 2 = 6\\), so we have \\(12 = 2 \\times 6\\).\n3. \\(6 \\div 2 = 3\\), so we have \\(6 = 2 \\times 3\\).\n4. \\(3 \\div 3 = 1\\), so we have \\(3 = 3 \\times 1\\).\n\nThus, the prime factorization of 24 is:\n\\[ 24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1 \\]\n\nTo find the number of positive divisors, we use the formula:\n\\[ \\text{Number of divisors} = (e_1 + 1)(e_2 + 1) \\ldots (e_n + 1) \\]\nwhere \\(e_1, e_2, \\ldots, e_n\\) are the exponents in the prime factorization.\n\nFor \\(24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\\):\n\\[ e_1 = 3 \\]\n\\[ e_2 = 1 \\]\n\nSo, the number of positive divisors is:\n\\[ (3 + 1)(1 + 1) = 4 \\times 2 = 8 \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of positive divisors of 24 is:\n\\[ \\boxed{8} \\]",
