      "text": "To find the number of positive divisors of \\(24\\), we start by determining its prime factorization. We know that:\n\n\\[\n24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\n\\]\n\nThe formula to find the number of positive divisors of a number \\(n\\) with the prime factorization \\(n = p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n(e_1 + 1)(e_2 + 1) \\cdots (e_k + 1)\n\\]\n\nFor \\(24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\\), the exponents are \\(3\\) and \\(1\\). Applying the formula, the number of positive divisors is:\n\n\\[\n(3 + 1)(1 + 1) = 4 \\times 2 = 8\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of positive divisors of \\(24\\) is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).",
